<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05C7">Remark <span data-tag="05C7">4.8.5.12</span>.</a> Let $F: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be a functor of $\infty $-categories. It follows from Remark <a data-tag="05C3" href="/tag/05C3">4.8.5.5</a> (and Theorem <a data-tag="01JX" href="/tag/01JX">4.8.4.1</a>) that if $F$ is categorically $(n+1)$-connective, then the induced map of homotopy $n$-categories $\operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}})}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}_{\mathit{\leq {}n}}{\mathit{(\operatorname{\mathcal{D}})}}$ is an equivalence. In particular, if $F$ is categorically $2$-connective, then it induces an equivalence of homotopy categories $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \rightarrow \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}$. </p>
